mission "The Battle of Lantern Passage"
    name "The Battle of Lantern Passage"
    description "Defeat the syndicate's hired escort squadron before it can seize the scholar's charts."
    source "Saint Brigid"
    destination "Port de Lune"
    reward 1980
    speaker offer "Commodore Wycliffe"
    speaker visit "Commodore Wycliffe"
    speaker complete "Commodore Wycliffe"
    to offer
        has "The Company Beneath the Sand: done"
    objective kills 2
    battlefield "Lantern Passage" 9000 3200
    enemy "Wycliffe's Vanguard"
    enemy "Wycliffe's Second"
    on offer
        conversation
            `The scholar's charts are being moved under guard at Lantern Passage. A hired squadron has taken station across the channel, close enough to seize the papers before the survey ships can clear the harbour.`
            `Commodore Wycliffe watches the squadron through a spyglass. "The syndicate has hired warships to take the charts. They do not need the islands if they can own the only route into them. I need that squadron broken before the papers change hands."`
            choice
                `"I will help you get to the bottom of it."`
                    accept
                `"Who else knows about this?"`
                    goto details
                `"I will leave this to a captain with fewer reservations."`
                    close
            label details
                `Wycliffe points to the chart boats. "Keep the channel open for the scholars. Scatter the escorts before they can close around the boats; the papers matter more than a chase after every fleeing ship."`
                choice
                    `"I will take the risk. Put the destination on my chart."`
                        accept
                    `"I have other waters to cross. Good day."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Battle of Lantern Passage. Defeat the syndicate's hired escort squadron before it can seize the scholar's charts."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Port de Lune, Wycliffe counts the returned charts and confirms that the hired squadron has been driven off. "They came for the papers, not the harbour," he says. "That tells us who is truly afraid of what the scholars have found."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Wycliffe secures the charts in a dispatch case. "The papers are safe, and the syndicate has lost its hired screen. A ship can be replaced. A record, once burned, is gone. You understood which was worth defending."`
        log "Completed The Battle of Lantern Passage. Received 1980 gold. Defeat the syndicate's hired escort squadron before it can seize the scholar's charts."
